sequenceDiagram
  participant UI as React SPA
  participant Routes as REST Route Layer
  participant Session as Session/Role Resolver
  participant Policy as SoD Policy
  participant EntrySvc as Journal Entry Service
  participant EntryRepo as Entry Repository
  participant HistRepo as History Repository (insert-only)

  Note over UI,HistRepo: Scenario 1 - submit a balanced draft
  UI->>Routes: POST /api/finance/entries/{id}/submit
  Routes->>Session: resolve caller identity and roles
  Session-->>Routes: {userId, roles:[accountant]}
  Routes->>Policy: authorise(submit, caller, entry.creatorId)
  Policy-->>Routes: allowed
  Routes->>EntrySvc: submit(entryId)
  EntrySvc->>EntryRepo: load entry + lines
  EntryRepo-->>EntrySvc: entry{status:draft, lines, balanced:true}
  EntrySvc->>EntrySvc: verify status=draft and balance check passes
  EntrySvc->>EntryRepo: update status=submitted
  EntryRepo-->>EntrySvc: ok
  EntrySvc->>HistRepo: append {entryId, action:submit, by:userId, at:now}
  HistRepo-->>EntrySvc: appended
  EntrySvc-->>Routes: entry{status:submitted}
  Routes-->>UI: 200 {entry}

  Note over UI,HistRepo: Scenario 2 - creator attempts edit after submission
  UI->>Routes: PATCH /api/finance/entries/{id}/lines/{lineId} {amount}
  Routes->>Session: resolve caller identity and roles
  Session-->>Routes: {userId=creator, roles:[accountant]}
  Routes->>Policy: authorise(editLine, caller, entry.creatorId)
  Policy-->>Routes: allowed (creator may normally edit own entries)
  Routes->>EntrySvc: updateLine(entryId, lineId, amount)
  EntrySvc->>EntryRepo: load entry
  EntryRepo-->>EntrySvc: entry{status:submitted}
  EntrySvc->>EntrySvc: status != draft -> reject edit
  EntrySvc-->>Routes: error LOCKED_FOR_EDITING
  Routes-->>UI: 409 {error:"entry is submitted and locked"}
  Note right of EntryRepo: stored entry and lines unchanged
